From 070547c9922415850a220ab260eff040e28e46bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emergent-agent-e1 <github@emergent.sh>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:58:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(private-mode): field-confirmation timestamp robustness
 (get_time) + new-cycle state reset

Root cause (field test 18.09.2026, FMC130 781479): _device_response_confirm read the entry
instant ONLY from e.get('time'). Navixy history can carry it in get_time (as elsewhere in
this codebase). With time absent, _parse(None)=None and the anti-stale filter dropped EVERY
real response -> PR#8 hardware-ACK matcher never reached -> UNKNOWN/TIMEOUT.

FIX (application code only, additive, gate/driver_id untouched):
- new _entry_time(entry) reads time|get_time|timestamp|event_time (tz-aware); used by
  _device_response_confirm. Anti-stale stays strict (no usable ts / older than command_sent_at
  -> refused; success False/error -> never; wrong mode -> refused). Telemetry fallback unchanged.
- request_mode: a NEW PRIVATE cycle explicitly purges the previous cycle's end/result fields
  before writing the new START (private_start_* + fresh anchor preserved through PRIVATE->BUSINESS;
  private_mileage_session history untouched).

Adds READ-ONLY diagnostic diagnostics/navixy_confirmation_diag_781479_0918.py.
Verified: confirmation suite 35/35 under BOTH gate regimes (LEGACY + account-model).
DEVICE_WRITE stays 0; no device command. Tests updates are handled separately.
